          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            Original articles introducing cobordism as a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead-generalized+cohomology+theory"} Whitehead-generalized cohomology theory
          %ul
            %li#Atiyah61
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Bordism and Cobordism
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004100035064"} doi:10.1017/S0305004100035064
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/atiyahb.pdf"} pdf
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (introducing the concept, with focus on
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSO"}> MSO
                  )
            %li#ConnerFloyd66
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Conner"}> Pierre Conner
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edwin+Floyd"} Edwin Floyd
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Relation+of+Cobordism+to+K-Theories"} The Relation of Cobordism to K-Theories
                %strong 28
                Springer 1966 (
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/BFb0071091"}> doi:10.1007/BFb0071091
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=216511"} MR216511
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (relating
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+cobordism+theory"} complex cobordism theory
                  to
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
                  and the
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/e-invariant"} e-invariant
            %li#Quillen71
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Quillen"}> Daniel Quillen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Elementary Proofs of Some Results of Cobordism Theory Using Steenrod Operations
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/0001-8708(71)90041-7"} doi:10.1016/0001-8708(71)90041-7
          %p Early survey:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Buchstaber"}> Victor Buchstaber
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cobordisms in problems of algebraic topology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01084983"} doi:10.1007/BF01084983
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Landweber"}> Peter Landweber
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A survey of bordism and cobordism
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004100066032"} doi:10.1017/S0305004100066032
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li#Stong68
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Stong"}> Robert Stong
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Notes on Cobordism theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://pi.math.virginia.edu/StongConf/Stongbookcontents.pdf"} toc pdf
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://press.princeton.edu/titles/6465.html"} ISBN:9780691649016
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/stongcob.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Rudyak98
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuli+Rudyak"}> Yuli Rudyak
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On Thom spectra, orientability and cobordism
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-77751-9"} doi:10.1007/978-3-540-77751-9
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~aar/papers/rudyakthom.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant
            versions:
          %ul
            %li#Cruickshank99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Cruickshank"}> James Cruickshank
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Twisted Cobordism and its Relationship to Equivariant Homotopy Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.collectionscanada.gc.ca/obj/s4/f2/dsk1/tape9/PQDD_0030/NQ46823.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Cruickshank99.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+Pontrjagin+theorem"} equivariant Pontrjagin theorem
                  for
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+actions"} free
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-manifolds"} G-manifolds
            %li#Cruickshank03
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Cruickshank"}> James Cruickshank
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Twisted homotopy theory and the geometric equivariant 1-stem
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0166-8641(02)00183-9"} arXiv:10.1016/S0166-8641(02)00183-9
          %div
            %h3#ReferencesPontrjaginThomConstruction Pontrjagin-Thom construction
            %h4#ReferencesPontrjaginConstruction Pontrjagin’s construction
            %h5#general General
            %p
              The
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin+theorem"} Pontryagin theorem
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normally+framed+submanifold"} framed
              version of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin-Thom+construction"} Pontrjagin-Thom construction
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+classes"} cobordism classes
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normally+framed+submanifolds"} normally framed submanifolds
              with their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cohomotopy+charge"} Cohomotopy charge
              in unstable
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karol+Borsuk"} Borsuk
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edwin+Spanier"} Spanier
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cohomotopy+sets"} Cohomotopy sets
            %ul
              %li#Pontryagin38a
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lev+Pontrjagin"}> Lev Pontrjagin
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Classification+of+continuous+maps+of+a+complex+into+a+sphere"} Classification of continuous maps of a complex into a sphere
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Communication I
                  %strong 19
                  3 (1938) 147-149
              %li#Pontryagin50
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lev+Pontryagin"}> Lev Pontryagin
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopy+classification+of+mappings+of+an+%28n%2B2%29-dimensional+sphere+on+an+n-dimensional+one"} Homotopy classification of mappings of an (n+2)-dimensional sphere on an n-dimensional one
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/pont3.pdf"} pdf
            %p
              (both available in English translation in
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "Revaz+Gamkrelidze#Gamkrelidze86"} Gamkrelidze 86
            %p as presented more comprehensively in:
            %ul
              %li#Pontryagin55
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lev+Pontrjagin"}> Lev Pontrjagin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth+manifolds+and+their+applications+in+Homotopy+theory"} Smooth manifolds and their applications in Homotopy theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.worldscientific.com/doi/abs/10.1142/9789812772107_0001"} doi:10.1142/9789812772107_0001
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/pont001.pdf"} pdf
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin+theorem"} Pontrjagin theorem
              must have been known to Pontrjagin at least by 1936, when he announced the computation of the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second+stable+homotopy+group+of+spheres"} second stem of homotopy groups of spheres
            %ul
              %li#Pontrjagin36
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lev+Pontrjagin"}> Lev Pontrjagin
                ,
                %em Sur les transformations des sphères en sphères
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/PontrjaginSurLesTransformationDesSpheres.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                ) in:
                %em Comptes Rendus du Congrès International des Mathématiques – Oslo 1936
                (
                %a{:href => "https://www.mathunion.org/fileadmin/ICM/Proceedings/ICM1936.2/ICM1936.2.ocr.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %p Review:
            %ul
              %li#FreedUhlenbeck91
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karen+Uhlenbeck"} Karen Uhlenbeck
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Instantons and Four-Manifolds
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4613-9703-8"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4613-9703-8
              %li#Bredon93
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Glen+Bredon"}> Glen Bredon
                  , chapter II.16 of:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Topology and Geometry
                  = succeed "," do
                    %strong 139
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4757-6848-0"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4757-6848-0
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "http://virtualmath1.stanford.edu/~ralph/math215b/Bredon.pdf"} pdf
            %div{:style => "margin: -30px 0px 20px 10px"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/Bredon-FigII13-PontryaginThom.jpg", :width => "450px"}/
            %ul
              %li#Kosinski93
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Antoni+Kosinski"}> Antoni Kosinski
                  , chapter IX of:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Differential manifolds
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/kosinski.pdf"} pdf
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://www.sciencedirect.com/bookseries/pure-and-applied-mathematics/vol/138/suppl/C"} ISBN:978-0-12-421850-5
              %li#Milnor97
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Milnor"}> John Milnor
                  , Chapter 7 of:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Topology from the differentiable viewpoint
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://press.princeton.edu/books/paperback/9780691048338/topology-from-the-differentiable-viewpoint"} ISBN:9780691048338
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/milnortop.pdf"} pdf
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mladen+Bestvina"} Mladen Bestvina
                  (notes by
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adam+Keenan"} Adam Keenan
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Differentiable Topology and Geometry
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/BestvinaKeenanDifferentialTopology.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michel+Kervaire"}> Michel Kervaire
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em La méthode de Pontryagin pour la classification des applications sur une sphère
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Topologia Differenziale
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-10988-1_3"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-10988-1_3
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rustam+Sadykov"}> Rustam Sadykov
                  , Section 1 of:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Elements of Surgery Theory
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://www.math.ksu.edu/~sadykov/Lecture%20Notes/Surgery%20Theory.pdf"} pdf
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/SadykovSurgeryTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %li#Csepai20
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A1s+Cs%C3%A9pai"}> András Csépai
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Stable Pontryagin-Thom construction for proper maps
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1905.07734"} arXiv:1905.07734
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10998-020-00327-0"} doi:10.1007/s10998-020-00327-0
            %p Discussion of the early history:
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#Kosinski93"} Kosinski 93, Section IX.9
            %h5#TwistedEquivariantPontrjaginConstruction Twisted/equivariant generalizations
            %p
              The (fairly straightforward) generalization of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin+theorem"} Pontrjagin theorem
              to the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Pontrjagin+theorem"} twisted Pontrjagin theorem
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Cohomotopy"} twisted Cohomotopy
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+classes"} cobordism classes
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normally+twisted-framed+submanifolds"} normally twisted-framed submanifolds
            %ul
              %li#Cruickshank03
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Cruickshank"}> James Cruickshank
                , Lemma 5.2 using Sec. 5.1 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Twisted homotopy theory and the geometric equivariant 1-stem
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0166-8641(02)00183-9"} doi:10.1016/S0166-8641(02)00183-9
            %p
              A general
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+Pontrjagin+theorem"} equivariant Pontrjagin theorem
              – relating
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+Cohomotopy"} equivariant Cohomotopy
              to normal equivariant framed submanifolds – remains elusive, but on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} free
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-manifolds"} G-manifolds
              it is again straightforward (and reduces to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Pontrjagin+theorem"} twisted Pontrjagin theorem
              on the
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
            %ul
              %li#Cruickshank99
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Cruickshank"}> James Cruickshank
                , Thm. 5.0.6, Cor. 6.0.13 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Twisted Cobordism and its Relationship to Equivariant Homotopy Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.collectionscanada.gc.ca/obj/s4/f2/dsk1/tape9/PQDD_0030/NQ46823.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Cruickshank99.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %h5#InNegativeCodimension In negative codimension
            %p
              In
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negative+number"} negative
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cohomotopy+charge+map"} Cohomotopy charge map
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin+theorem"} Pontrjagin theorem
              gives the
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "configuration+space+of+points#LoopSpacesOfSuspensions"} May-Segal theorem
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cohomotopy"} Cohomotopy
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle+spaces"} cocycle spaces
              with
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+spaces+of+points"} configuration spaces of points
            %ul
              %li#May72
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"}> Peter May
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em The geometry of iterated loop spaces
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/BOOKS/geom_iter.pdf"} pdf
              %li#Segal73
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Configuration-spaces and iterated loop-spaces
                  %strong 21
                  (1973), 213–221. MR 0331377 (
                  %a{:href => "http://dodo.pdmi.ras.ru/~topology/books/segal.pdf"}> pdf
                  )
                %p c Generalization of these constructions and results is due to
              %li#McDuff75
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dusa+McDuff"}> Dusa McDuff
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Configuration spaces of positive and negative particles
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0040-9383(75)90038-5"} doi:10.1016/0040-9383(75)90038-5
              %li#Boedigheimer87
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carl-Friedrich+B%C3%B6digheimer"}> Carl-Friedrich Bödigheimer
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Stable splittings of mapping spaces
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-bonn.de/~cfb/PUBLICATIONS/stable-splittings-of-mapping-spaces.pdf"} pdf
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/BoedigheimerStableSplittings87.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %h4#thoms_construction Thom’s construction
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom%27s+theorem"} Thom's theorem
              i.e. the unstable and
              %em oriented
              version of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin-Thom+construction"} Pontrjagin-Thom construction
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+classes"} cobordism classes
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normally+oriented+submanifolds"} normally oriented submanifolds
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+classes"} homotopy classes
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maps"} maps
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+vector+bundle"} universal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+orthogonal+group"} special orthogonal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+space"} Thom space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mi SO
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M SO(n)
            %ul
              %li#Thom54
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ren%C3%A9+Thom"}> René Thom
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quelques+propri%C3%A9t%C3%A9s+globales+des+vari%C3%A9t%C3%A9s+diff%C3%A9rentiables"} Quelques propriétés globales des variétés différentiables
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02566923"} doi:10.1007/BF02566923
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://eudml.org/doc/139072"} dml:139072
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.digizeitschriften.de/dms/img/?PID=GDZPPN002056259"} digiz:GDZPPN002056259
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/thomcob.pdf"} pdf
            %p Textbook accounts:
            %ul
              %li#Stong68
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Stong"}> Robert Stong
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Notes on Cobordism theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://pi.math.virginia.edu/StongConf/Stongbookcontents.pdf"} toc pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://press.princeton.edu/titles/6465.html"} publisher page
            %h4#lashofs_construction Lashof’s construction
            %p
              The joint generalization of
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#Pontryagin38a"} Pontryagin 38a
              %a{:href => "#Pontryagin55"} 55
              (framing structure) and
              %a{:href => "#Thom54"} Thom 54
              (orientation structure) to any family of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangential+structures"} tangential structures
              (“
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28B%2Cf%29-structure"}> (B,f)-structure
              ”) is first made explicit in
            %ul
              %li#Lashof63
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Lashof"}> Richard Lashof
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Poincaré duality and cobordism
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/S0002-9947-1963-0156357-4"} doi:10.1090/S0002-9947-1963-0156357-4
            %p
              and the general statement that has come to be known as the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin-Thom+isomorphism"} Pontryagin-Thom isomorphism
              (identifying the stable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+classes"} cobordism classes
              of normally
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangential+structure"} (B,f)-structured
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifolds"} submanifolds
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+classes"} homotopy classes
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maps"} maps
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mf"} Mf
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Lashof63"} Lashof 63, Theorem C
            %p Textbook accounts:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theodor+Br%C3%B6cker"}> Theodor Bröcker
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tammo+tom+Dieck"} Tammo tom Dieck
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Kobordismentheorie
                  = succeed "," do
                    %strong 178
                  = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                    %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/9783540053415"} ISBN:9783540053415
              %li#Kochman96
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stanley+Kochman"}> Stanley Kochman
                  , section 1.5 of:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bordism%2C+Stable+Homotopy+and+Adams+Spectral+Sequences"} Bordism, Stable Homotopy and Adams Spectral Sequences
              %li#Rudyak98
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuli+Rudyak"}> Yuli Rudyak
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em On Thom spectra, orientability and cobordism
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-77751-9"} doi:10.1007/978-3-540-77751-9
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~aar/papers/rudyakthom.pdf"} pdf
            %p Lecture notes:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Francis"}> John Francis
                  ,
                  %em Topology of manifolds
                  course notes (2010) (
                  %a{:href => "http://math.northwestern.edu/~jnkf/classes/mflds/"}> web
                  ), Lecture 3:
                  %em Thom’s theorem
                  (
                  %a{:href => "http://math.northwestern.edu/~jnkf/classes/mflds/3thom.pdf"}> pdf
                  ), Lecture 4
                  %em Transversality
                  (notes by I. Bobkova) (
                  %a{:href => "http://math.northwestern.edu/~jnkf/classes/mflds/4transversality.pdf"}> pdf
                  )
              %li#Malkiewich11
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cary+Malkiewich"}> Cary Malkiewich
                  , Section 3 of:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      Unoriented cobordism and
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi M
                            %mi O
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M O
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://math.uiuc.edu/~cmalkiew/cobordism.pdf"} pdf
              %li
                %p
                  Tom Weston, Part I of
                  %em An introduction to cobordism theory
                  (
                  %a{:href => "http://people.math.umass.edu/~weston/oldpapers/cobord.pdf"}> pdf
                  )
            %p See also:
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Manifold+Atlas"}> Manifold Atlas
                ,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://www.map.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/B-Bordism#The_Pontrjagin-Thom_isomorphism"} The Pontrjagin-Thom isomorphism
          %h3#relation_to_divisors Relation to divisors
          %p
            Relation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+cobordism+cohomology"} complex cobordism cohomology
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/divisors"} divisors
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+cycles"} algebraic cycles
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chow+groups"} Chow groups
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Burt+Totaro"}> Burt Totaro
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Torsion algebraic cycles and complex cobordism
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/S0894-0347-97-00232-4"} doi:10.1090/S0894-0347-97-00232-4
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/a/272131/381"} MO discussion
